<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnĕrārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a gift</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Var. 6,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to gladiatorial
				exhibitions</i> (a word first used by Augustus, acc. to <i><span class="en">Quint. 8,
				3, 34</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: libellus, Trebell.
				<i><span class="en">Claud. 5,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnĕrārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>One who bestows gifts</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pauperum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 66, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>The giver of a gladiatorial exhibition</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thracem mirmilloni parem, munerario imparem
					dixerat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 4 praef.</span></i>; Inscr Orell.
			1185; 2534; 2585; 3746.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
